card.statement:
Applying Theorem <<ref:kju>> and Corollary <<ref:jmo>> to complex and real matrix representations of the quivers

\[
\xymatrix{
*{\ci}
\ar@(ur,dr)}
\qquad     \qquad \qquad      \qquad
\xymatrix{
{\ci}
\ar@(u,r)
\save !<-1pt,0.5pt>
\ar@(l,u)\restore
\ar@(d,l)
\save[]+<2ex,-0.8ex>*
{\cdot}
\restore
\save[]+<1.6ex,-1.7ex>*
{\cdot}
\restore
\save[]+<0.7ex,-2ex>*
{\cdot}
\restore
}
\qquad \qquad      \qquad
\xymatrix{
*{\ci}
\ar@/^1.2pc/[rr]
\ar@/^0.6pc/[rr]
\ar@/_1.2pc/[rr]
&\save[]+<0ex,-0.3pc>*
{\vdots}
\restore&
*{\ci}}
\]

we get Specht's, Wiegmann's, and Jing's criteria (see the beginning of Section <<ref:intr>>).
